"""
    pw_core_events

` pw_core_events`

Core events

| Field         | Note                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |
| :------------ | :--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| info          | Notify new core info  This event is emitted when first bound to the core or when the hello method is called.  # Arguments * `info`: new core info                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |
| done          | Emit a done event  The done event is emitted as a result of a sync method with the same seq number.  # Arguments * `seq`: the seq number passed to the sync method call                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |
| ping          | Emit a ping event  The client should reply with a pong reply with the same seq number.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |
| error         | Fatal error event  The error event is sent out when a fatal (non-recoverable) error has occurred. The id argument is the proxy object where the error occurred, most often in response to a request to that object. The message is a brief description of the error, for (debugging) convenience.  This event is usually also emitted on the proxy object with *id*.  # Arguments * `id`: object where the error occurred * `seq`: the sequence number that generated the error * `res`: error code * `message`: error description |
| remove\\_id   | Remove an object ID  This event is used internally by the object ID management logic. When a client deletes an object, the server will send this event to acknowledge that it has seen the delete request. When the client receives this event, it will know that it can safely reuse the object ID.  # Arguments * `id`: deleted object ID                                                                                                                                                                                        |
| bound\\_id    | Notify an object binding  This event is emitted when a local object ID is bound to a global ID. It is emitted before the global becomes visible in the registry.  The bound\\_props event is an enhanced version of this event that also contains the extra global properties.  # Arguments * `id`: bound object ID * `global_id`: the global id bound to                                                                                                                                                                          |
| add\\_mem     | Add memory for a client  Memory is given to a client as *fd* of a certain memory *type*.  Further references to this fd will be made with the per memory unique identifier *id*.  # Arguments * `id`: the unique id of the memory * `type`: the memory type, one of enum [`spa_data_type`](@ref) * `fd`: the file descriptor * `flags`: extra flags                                                                                                                                                                                |
| remove\\_mem  | Remove memory for a client  # Arguments * `id`: the memory id to remove                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |
| bound\\_props | Notify an object binding  This event is emitted when a local object ID is bound to a global ID. It is emitted before the global becomes visible in the registry.  This is an enhanced version of the bound\\_id event.  Since version 4:1  # Arguments * `id`: bound object ID * `global_id`: the global id bound to * `props`: The properties of the new global object.                                                                                                                                                           |
"""
struct pw_core_events
    version::UInt32
    info::Ptr{Cvoid}
    done::Ptr{Cvoid}
    ping::Ptr{Cvoid}
    error::Ptr{Cvoid}
    remove_id::Ptr{Cvoid}
    bound_id::Ptr{Cvoid}
    add_mem::Ptr{Cvoid}
    remove_mem::Ptr{Cvoid}
    bound_props::Ptr{Cvoid}
end

"""
    pw_core_methods

` pw_core_methods`

Core methods

The core global object. This is a singleton object used for creating new objects in the remote PipeWire instance. It is also used for internal features.

| Field           | Note                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |
| :-------------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| hello           | Start a conversation with the server. This will send the core info and will destroy all resources for the client (except the core and client resource).  This requires X permissions on the core.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |
| sync            | Do server roundtrip  Ask the server to emit the 'done' event with *seq*.  Since methods are handled in-order and events are delivered in-order, this can be used as a barrier to ensure all previous methods and the resulting events have been handled.  This requires X permissions on the core.  # Arguments * `seq`: the seq number passed to the done event                                                                                                                                                                |
| pong            | Reply to a server ping event.  Reply to the server ping event with the same seq.  This requires X permissions on the core.  # Arguments * `seq`: the seq number received in the ping event                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |
| error           | Fatal error event  The error method is sent out when a fatal (non-recoverable) error has occurred. The id argument is the proxy object where the error occurred, most often in response to an event on that object. The message is a brief description of the error, for (debugging) convenience.  This method is usually also emitted on the resource object with *id*.  This requires X permissions on the core.  # Arguments * `id`: resource id where the error occurred * `res`: error code * `message`: error description |
| get\\_registry  | Get the registry object  Create a registry object that allows the client to list and bind the global objects available from the PipeWire server  This requires X permissions on the core.  # Arguments * `version`: the client version * `user_data_size`: extra size                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |
| create\\_object | Create a new object on the PipeWire server from a factory.  This requires X permissions on the core.  # Arguments * `factory_name`: the factory name to use * `type`: the interface to bind to * `version`: the version of the interface * `props`: extra properties * `user_data_size`: extra size                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |
| destroy         | Destroy an resource  Destroy the server resource for the given proxy.  This requires X permissions on the core.  # Arguments * `obj`: the proxy to destroy                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |
"""
struct pw_core_methods
    version::UInt32
    add_listener::Ptr{Cvoid}
    hello::Ptr{Cvoid}
    sync::Ptr{Cvoid}
    pong::Ptr{Cvoid}
    error::Ptr{Cvoid}
    get_registry::Ptr{Cvoid}
    create_object::Ptr{Cvoid}
    destroy::Ptr{Cvoid}
end

mutable struct pw_core end

