"""
    spa_io_type

Different IO area types

| Enumerator              | Note                                                                                 |
| :---------------------- | :----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| SPA\\_IO\\_Buffers      | area to exchange buffers, struct [`spa_io_buffers`](@ref)                            |
| SPA\\_IO\\_Range        | expected byte range, struct [`spa_io_range`](@ref) (currently not used in PipeWire)  |
| SPA\\_IO\\_Clock        | area to update clock information, struct [`spa_io_clock`](@ref)                      |
| SPA\\_IO\\_Latency      | latency reporting, struct [`spa_io_latency`](@ref)                                   |
| SPA\\_IO\\_Control      | area for control messages, struct [`spa_io_sequence`](@ref)                          |
| SPA\\_IO\\_Notify       | area for notify messages, struct [`spa_io_sequence`](@ref)                           |
| SPA\\_IO\\_Position     | position information in the graph, struct [`spa_io_position`](@ref)                  |
| SPA\\_IO\\_RateMatch    | rate matching between nodes, struct [`spa_io_rate_match`](@ref)                      |
| SPA\\_IO\\_Memory       | memory pointer, struct [`spa_io_memory`](@ref) (currently not used in PipeWire)      |
| SPA\\_IO\\_AsyncBuffers | async area to exchange buffers, struct [`spa_io_async_buffers`](@ref)                |
"""
const spa_io_type = UInt32
const SPA_IO_Invalid = 0 % UInt32
const SPA_IO_Buffers = 1 % UInt32
const SPA_IO_Range = 2 % UInt32
const SPA_IO_Clock = 3 % UInt32
const SPA_IO_Latency = 4 % UInt32
const SPA_IO_Control = 5 % UInt32
const SPA_IO_Notify = 6 % UInt32
const SPA_IO_Position = 7 % UInt32
const SPA_IO_RateMatch = 8 % UInt32
const SPA_IO_Memory = 9 % UInt32
const SPA_IO_AsyncBuffers = 10 % UInt32

"""
    spa_io_buffers

IO area to exchange buffers.

A set of buffers should first be configured on the node/port. Further references to those buffers will be made by using the id of the buffer.

If status is [`SPA_STATUS_OK`](@ref), the host should ignore the io area.

If status is [`SPA_STATUS_NEED_DATA`](@ref), the host should: 1) recycle the buffer in buffer\\_id, if possible 2) prepare a new buffer and place the id in buffer\\_id.

If status is [`SPA_STATUS_HAVE_DATA`](@ref), the host should consume the buffer in buffer\\_id and set the state to [`SPA_STATUS_NEED_DATA`](@ref) when new data is requested.

If status is [`SPA_STATUS_STOPPED`](@ref), some error occurred on the port.

If status is [`SPA_STATUS_DRAINED`](@ref), data from the io area was used to drain.

Status can also be a negative errno value to indicate errors. such as: -EINVAL: buffer\\_id is invalid -EPIPE: no more buffers available

| Field       | Note             |
| :---------- | :--------------- |
| status      | the status code  |
| buffer\\_id | a buffer id      |
"""
struct spa_io_buffers
    status::Int32
    buffer_id::UInt32
end

