"""
    spa_io_clock

Absolute time reporting.

Nodes that can report clocking information will receive this io block. The application sets the id. This is usually set as part of the position information but can also be set separately.

The clock counts the elapsed time according to the clock provider since the provider was last started.

Driver nodes are supposed to update the contents of SPA_IO_Clock before signaling the start of a graph cycle. These updated clock values become visible to other nodes in SPA_IO_Position. Non-driver nodes do not need to update the contents of their SPA_IO_Clock. Also see page_driver for further details.

The host generally gives each node a separate spa_io_clock in SPA_IO_Clock, so that updates made by the driver are not visible in the contents of SPA_IO_Clock of other nodes. Instead, SPA_IO_Position is used to look up the current graph time.

A node is a driver when spa_io_clock::id and the ID in spa_io_position.clock in SPA_IO_Position are the same.

The flags are set by the graph driver at the start of each cycle.

| Field             | Note                                                                                                                                                                                                               |
| :---------------- | :----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| flags             | Clock flags                                                                                                                                                                                                        |
| id                | Unique clock id, set by host application                                                                                                                                                                           |
| name              | Clock name prefixed with API, set by node when it receives SPA_IO_Clock. The clock name is unique per clock and can be used to check if nodes share the same clock.                                                |
| nsec              | Time in nanoseconds against monotonic clock (CLOCK\\_MONOTONIC). This fields reflects a real time instant in the past, when the current cycle started. The value may have jitter.                                  |
| rate              | Rate for position/duration/delay/xrun                                                                                                                                                                              |
| position          | Current position, in samples @ rate                                                                                                                                                                                |
| duration          | Duration of current cycle, in samples @ rate                                                                                                                                                                       |
| delay             | Delay between position and hardware, in samples @ rate                                                                                                                                                             |
| rate\\_diff       | Rate difference between clock and monotonic time, as a ratio of clock speeds. A value higher than 1.0 means that the driver's internal clock is faster than the monotonic clock (by that factor), and vice versa.  |
| next\\_nsec       | Estimated next wakeup time in nanoseconds. This time is a logical start time of the next cycle, and is not necessarily in the future.                                                                              |
| target\\_rate     | Target rate of next cycle                                                                                                                                                                                          |
| target\\_duration | Target duration of next cycle                                                                                                                                                                                      |
| target\\_seq      | Seq counter. must be equal at start and end of read and lower bit must be 0                                                                                                                                        |
| cycle             | incremented each time the graph is started                                                                                                                                                                         |
| xrun              | Estimated accumulated xrun duration                                                                                                                                                                                |
"""
struct spa_io_clock
    flags::UInt32
    id::UInt32
    name::NTuple{64, Cchar}
    nsec::UInt64
    rate::spa_fraction
    position::UInt64
    duration::UInt64
    delay::Int64
    rate_diff::Cdouble
    next_nsec::UInt64
    target_rate::spa_fraction
    target_duration::UInt64
    target_seq::UInt32
    cycle::UInt32
    xrun::UInt64
end

